urname>Matinaho</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>von Bonsdorff</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Rouhiainen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>L&#x000f6;nnroth</surname><given-names> M</given-names></name><name><surname>Parkkinen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dependence of Staphylococcus epidermidis on non-transferrin-bound iron for growth</article-title><source>FEMS Microbiol Lett</source><year>2003</year><volume>196</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11267776</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>von Bonsdorff</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sahlstedt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ebeling</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruutu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Parkkinen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Apotransferrin administration prevents growth of Staphylococcus epidermidis in serum of stem cell transplant patients by binding of free iron</article-title><source>FEMS Immunol Med Microbiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12770759</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aguila</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrera</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrison</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cosgrove</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Perojo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Montesinos</surname><given-names>I</given-names><